Privacy Policy
Long Night: To Tomorrow · Effective date: October 12, 2026
 
In short: Long Night: To Tomorrow does not collect, store on our servers, share or sell any personal data. The game works fully offline and keeps your progress only on your own device.
 
1. Who we are
“Long Night: To Tomorrow” (also published as “Uzun Gece”, the “Game”) is developed and published by Vainsteel Studios, Ankara, Türkiye (“we”, “us”). This policy applies to the Game on iOS, iPadOS and Android.
 
2. Data we collect
We do not collect any personal data. The Game has no account system, no sign-in, no advertising, no in-app purchases and no analytics or tracking tools that send data anywhere. We do not collect your name, e-mail address, phone number, contacts, location, photos, device identifiers or advertising identifiers.
 
3. Data stored on your device
Your save (current day, choices, relationships, money and items) is stored only in the Game's local storage on your device. It is never sent to us.
Your settings (language, sound and volume, text size, contrast, reduced motion, text speed and untimed minigames) are also stored only on your device.
The Game keeps simple play statistics (for example which scenes you reached, number of sessions and active play time) inside your save on your device. They are never sent anywhere.
“Export save” and “Error report” only show text on your screen and, when you tap “Copy save” or “Copy report”, place it on your device's clipboard. Nothing is sent automatically; you decide whether to paste or share that text with anyone.
 
4. Internet access and permissions
The Game does not need an internet connection and does not contact any server while you play. All game files are included in the app. It does not request access to your camera, microphone, location, contacts or photos. On Android the standard internet permission is present because the app framework includes it; the Game does not use it to send data.
 
5. Sharing and selling of data
Because we do not collect personal data, we do not share, sell or rent any personal data to third parties, and we do not use your data for advertising or profiling.
 
6. Children
The Game is intended for a general audience and does not knowingly collect personal data from anyone, including children under 13 (or the equivalent minimum age in your country).
 
7. Data retention and deletion
All game data stays on your device until you delete it. You can delete it at any time by deleting the Game or clearing its data in your device settings. Deleting the Game also deletes your progress; use Settings → Export save to copy your save first if you want to keep it.
 
8. Your rights
Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct or delete personal data. Since we do not hold any personal data about you, there is normally nothing for us to access or delete, but you are welcome to contact us with any question.
 
9. Fiction
The city of Veyra and all people, places, organisations and events in the Game are fictional.
 
10. Changes to this policy
If we change this policy (for example if a future version adds new features), we will update this page and the effective date above before the change takes effect.
 
